  "full_response": "# **The Complete History of Artificial Intelligence: From the 1950s to Present Day**\n\n## **Table of Contents**\n1. **Introduction to Artificial Intelligence**\n2. **The Birth of AI (1950s – Early Foundations)**\n   - The Dartmouth Conference (1956)\n   - Early AI Programs: Logic Theorist and General Problem Solver\n   - Key Figures: Alan Turing, John McCarthy, Marvin Minsky, Allen Newell, Herbert Simon\n3. **The Golden Age of AI (1960s – Early Optimism)**\n   - Symbolic AI and Early Expert Systems\n   - ELIZA: The First Chatbot\n   - The Rise of Machine Learning Concepts\n   - Challenges and the First AI Winter\n4. **The AI Winter (1970s – Early 1980s)**\n   - Funding Cuts and Skepticism\n   - Expert Systems and the Return of AI\n   - Japan’s Fifth Generation Computer Project\n5. **The Revival of AI (1980s – 1990s)**\n   - The Rise of Machine Learning\n   - Backpropagation and Neural Networks\n   - IBM’s Deep Blue Defeats Garry Kasparov (1997)\n6. **The Modern Era of AI (2000s – 2010s)**\n   - Big Data and the Rise of Deep Learning\n   - Geoffrey Hinton and the Deep Learning Revolution\n   - IBM Watson Wins Jeopardy! (2011)\n   - The Emergence of AI in Everyday Life\n7. **The Deep Learning Boom (2012 – Present)**\n   - AlexNet and the ImageNet Revolution (2012)\n   - Generative Adversarial Networks (GANs)\n   - Reinforcement Learning and AlphaGo (2016)\n   - Transformers and the Rise of Large Language Models (LLMs)\n8. **AI in the 2020s: Breakthroughs and Ethical Concerns**\n   - GPT-3 and the Rise of Foundation Models\n   - AI in Healthcare, Finance, and Autonomous Systems\n   - Ethical AI and Regulation\n   - The Future of AI: AGI and Beyond\n9. **Conclusion: The Evolution of AI and What Lies Ahead**\n\n---\n\n## **1. Introduction to Artificial Intelligence**\n\nArtificial Intelligence (AI) is the field of computer",
